  "interpretation": "Every arm has a quantization table, so QT-Norm stays in the JPEG domain. The luma and chroma table features match because the DQT is the same. q[3] is 1 only when Pillow get_sampling returns 2, which is 4:2:0. 4:4:4, 4:2:2, and 4:4:0 therefore produce the same q and the same FiLM gamma and beta. The header does not distinguish horizontal-only from vertical-only subsampling."
